<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Paranagua/Santos sugar shipping conditions.</title>
<headline>Brazil Paranagua/Santos sugar shipping conditions.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brazilian ports of</p>
<p>Paranagua and Santos reported the following conditions for</p>
<p>shipping sugar.</p>
<p>PARANAGUA:</p>
<p>No data available due to a computer fault.</p>
<p>SANTOS:</p>
<p>Vessels: All vessels at public terminals paralyzed due to a strike by administrative portworkers, including eight veseels loading bagged sugar and one loading bulk sugar. Waiting to dock, two vessels to load bulk sugar and three to load sugar (unspecified). At Cargill private terminal, Woodpecker loading</p>
<p>16,000 tonnes bulk sugar. No vessels waiting to dock.</p>
<p>Stocks: No figures available due to strike.</p>
<p>((--Joelle Diderich, Sao Paulo newsroom +55 11 248 5417))</p>
